# A rear-engined GT racing car, of the size and power the GT3 class runs: a six-cylinder engine
# behind the rear axle making about 400 kW, a six-speed sequential gearbox, a 2.5 m wheelbase,
# and 59% of its weight on the rear axle. It is test data for the vehicle model, and the tests
# that drive it (rear_engined.rs, keys.rs) hold it to what such a car does.

mass 1330                          # with its driver and fuel
inertia 1650 1800 520              # pitch, yaw, roll
centre 0 0.4 0.226                 # 59% of its weight on the rear axle
body 1.96 0.95 4.55 at 0 0.67 0

front at=1.25 track=1.70 radius=0.34 inertia=1.5 driven=no
front spring=110000 bump=6800 rebound=10000 bar=38000 travel=0.065,0.075 roll_centre=0.03
front brake=3100 grip=1
rear at=1.25 track=1.72 radius=0.355 inertia=2.0 driven=yes
rear spring=179000 bump=10400 rebound=14500 bar=16000 travel=0.07,0.08 roll_centre=0.08
rear brake=2500 grip=1.07          # the rear tyres are wider, and carry more

engine idle=1100 limit=9000 inertia=0.11 friction=30,0.01
torque 1500 278
torque 2000 317
torque 3000 374
torque 4000 422
torque 5000 461
torque 6000 480
torque 6500 485
torque 7000 480
torque 7500 472
torque 8000 463
torque 8400 454                    # 400 kW here
torque 8800 430
torque 9250 398
torque 9600 346

gears 3.34 2.5 1.95 1.58 1.31 1.113
final 3.9
reverse 3
gearbox shift=0.05 efficiency=0.93 clutch=900
diff preload=80 power=0.5 coast=0.35

aero drag=0.95 downforce=2.1 balance=0.36
steering lock=26 ackermann=0.6
geometry anti_dive=0.25 anti_squat=0.35
assists abs=yes traction=yes stability=yes
